          content: `## Describing People

**Physical appearance:** tall, short, thin, heavy, young, old, blonde, curly hair
**Character:** funny, serious, brave, shy, kind, clever, hard-working, talkative

*She is young and thin and has beautiful blonde hair.*
*He is the most hard-working student in our class.*

## Comparatives and Superlatives

| Adjective | Comparative | Superlative |
|-----------|-------------|-------------|
| tall | taller | the tallest |
| big | bigger | the biggest |
| beautiful | more beautiful | the most beautiful |
| good | better | the best |
| bad | worse | the worst |

*Mount Everest is the highest mountain in the world.*
*Sports cars are faster than normal cars.*

## Modal Verbs: will / would

**will** — for offers, promises, predictions, decisions:
- *I will help you carry that.* (offer)
- *It will rain tomorrow.* (prediction)
- *Will you come with me?* (invitation)

**would** — for polite requests and invitations:
- *Would you like some tea?*
- *Would you help me with this?*`,
